{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1487789-an-alternative-techn\u00e9-merit","id":1487789,"title":"An alternative Techn\u00e9 merit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-24T15:05:34-07:00","id":1487789,"title":"An alternative Techn\u00e9 merit","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">The idea behind Techn\u00e9 itself is fascinating, human culture contains glimpses of Supernal Truth and creativity creates new symbols. Because of that, incorporating not only the technology, but the culture itself into one\u2019s spellcasting can have a powerful effect. Unfortunately, this is not fully reflected in the mechanics. This is an attempt to make a version that has a comparable level of utility as other Order merits (<i>Lex Magica</i>, <i>Masque</i>, <i>Prelacies</i>, etc) while incentivizing a playstyle resonant with the themes of the Free Council. Design notes will also be included at the end, feedback is very welcome.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Techn\u00e9 (</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u25cf\u25cf</span>)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Requirements:</i> Free Council Order Status (<span style=\"font-size:11px\">\u25cf</span>)<br /> <br /> <i>Description:</i> Your character uses Libertine practices in order to use cultural magical styles, sciences, and art forms as magical tools. Pick a focus for your character \u2014 for example, computer networking. The mage learns how to draw upon the Supernal symbolism of their connections related to the chosen focus, granting them the ability to use social merits related to that field (Contacts, Allies, Staff, etc) as Investiture yantras, which provide a bonus equal to half their merit dots, rounded up.<br /> <br /> In addition, when the mage casts a non-obvious spell or participates in a team casting one, their own rolls benefit from nearby Sleepers engaging in their chosen focus. If a few Sleepers are present, it gains the 9-again quality. A large group instead grants 8-again and a large crowd provides the rote quality.<br /> <br /> Lastly, when all members of a teamwork spell have this Merit with the same focus, they do not suffer penalties for unplanned rituals.<br /> <br /> This merit can be taken multiple times to reflect different fields of study.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>What were you thinking design wise ?</b></span><br /> <br /> The first step to revise the merit is to analyze what already exists. Since there is no 1ed equivalent, this is very easy.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Techn\u00e9 (2ed) (</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u25cf\u25cf</span>)</span></span><br /> <i>Requirements:</i> Free Council Order Status (<span style=\"font-size:11px\">\u25cf</span>)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Description:</i> The mage chooses a focus, such as computer networking, and treats it as an Order tool. Sleepers using the focus can also be treated as Order tools, so long as the spell is not obvious. When all mages casting a cooperative spell have this merit and share the same focus, the spell gains 8-again. This merit can be bought multiple times to reflect multiple foci.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Analysis</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The merit builds up on the main thesis of the Free Council: human culture is magical. The benefit is given at 3 levels: when using the cultural practice as a yantra, when others are practicing the cultural activity and when cooperating with others using the same cultural focus.<br /> <br /> The benefit for using the foci or being amongst Sleepers using it is set at +1, which is not very good for a 2 dot merit. Using High Speech is a more efficient yantra, as are runes, neither of which are restricted to non-obvious spells.<br /> <br /> In the case of merits, having a Broad Dedication of that foci can be more helpful, allowing for a reduction of Paradox for one less XP point. A Shadow Name which includes the chosen foci can provide a higher yantra bonus and its symbolism can include a wider breadth of compatible yantras.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the 8-again benefit on teamwork rolls is the most interesting, but also the most restrictive. When the cabal is not composed of Libertines, it would require an investment of 3 merit dots, one for Order Status in the Free Council and two for the merit, in addition to choosing the same foci. Since there are more beneficial options for the same cost, there is little incentive to commit.<br /> <br /> Overall the cost benefit is not the best and it has less utility compared to other Order merits.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Revised Techn\u00e9 (</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u25cf\u25cf</span>)</span></span><br /> <i>Requirements:</i> Free Council Order Status (<span style=\"font-size:11px\">\u25cf</span>)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>Description:</i> Your character uses Libertine practices in order to use cultural magical styles, sciences, and art forms as magical tools. Pick a focus for your character \u2014 for example, computer networking. The mage learns how to draw upon the Supernal symbolism of their connections related to the chosen focus, granting them the ability to use social merits related to that field (Contacts, Allies, Staff, etc) as Investiture yantras, which provide a bonus equal to half their merit dots, rounded up.<br /> <br /> In addition, when the mage casts a non-obvious spell or participates in a team casting one, their own rolls benefit from nearby Sleepers engaging in their chosen focus. If a few Sleepers are present, it gains the 9-again quality. A large group instead grants 8-again and a large crowd provides the rote quality.<br /> <br /> Lastly, when all members of a teamwork spell have this Merit with the same focus, they do not suffer penalties for unplanned rituals.<br /> <br /> This merit can be taken multiple times to reflect different fields of study.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Analysis</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Silver Ladder also has a very strong focus on Sleeper society, which makes them very alike to the Free Council. The main distinction is that where the former is hierarchical, the latter is democratic. This has led them to be in opposition in many subjects. But they have far more similarities, so I wanted to make this merit allude to that by mirroring the th\u00e9arch\u2019s own. The <i>Lex Magica</i> is a series of 3 benefits that build up to give them a powerful edge when pursuing their focus, which is the law that binds Pentacle society together. Similarly, Techn\u00e9 will be made to provide a series of benefits that build up to empower their spells using Sleeper culture.<br /> <br /> An <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950668-ideas-for-alternative-free-council-order-merit-needed?p=954282#post954282\"><span style=\"color:#1155cc\"><u>excellent style merit</u></span></a> written by PenDragon was used as an inspiration. Utilizing the presence of Sleepers as a reverse type of Paradox for non-obvious spells was an inspired idea. But providing them a role as a Dedicated Tool would cause a bit of overlap with <i>Egregore</i>, so that was avoided. The approach to yantras and teamwork spellcasting was expanded upon using the information <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> provided on Investiture yantras (found on page 53) and on coordinated spells (detailed on page 55).<br /> <br /> The first effect allows the mage to leverage their connections within the culture of the foci. The stronger their involvement, the greater the bonus. So a chef that has many contacts in the culinary world (or with ingredient providers) could gain the benefit, just as much as an engineer could from their research staff or a musician from having Allies with different specializations (sound engineering, specific instruments, etc).<br /> <br /> Its secondary purpose is to incentivize the mage to build upon the focus. Since they already have the merits, it's easier for them to get yantras related to their chosen field and more tempting to build magical tools based on it. The main drawback is that it requires additional investment of XP in order to provide multiple powerful yantras, but it rewards players for focusing on their mage\u2019s theme.<br /> <br /> The second effect expands on the original teamwork concept using PenDragon\u2019s idea. This incentivizes the cabal to utilize the foci whenever they want to prepare a powerful spell, showcasing the convenience of the Free Council\u2019s methodology. It has a built in logistical challenge of finding a place with enough Sleepers using the foci for the bonus the mage wants, which incentivizes them to organize events. There exists a risk of an Act of Hubris in case the mage exposes Sleepers to an overt spell. Paradox receives a bonus on overt spells that is equal to the one the mage gains on covert ones.<br /> <br /> The third effect brings them all together. When all participants have the merit and the foci, they can benefit from the powerful dice effect of having Sleepers nearby and suffer no drawbacks when trying to improvise a powerful ritual. So in the best case scenario, all participants could benefit from rote casting and receive no penalties on an untrained ritual, not to mention empower it with whatever social merits they already have. It also synergizes with a cabal that has a specific interest or a <i>Cabal Theme</i>, allowing them more ways to build upon it.<br /> <br /> The combination of these effects would make the Libertines the masters of teamwork spells by virtue of their all inclusive philosophy. Furthermore, since this is a 2 dot merit, it would incentivize them to learn additional fields that are tangential to their specialty, like a specialist in chemistry could also learn molecular gastronomy, allowing them to use any overlapping contacts. This incentivizes the Libertine to be a real Renaissance man, a true polymath that showcases the Supernal versatility of Sleeper culture.<br /> <br /> Hope you enjoyed reading this and thank you in advance for the feedback.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-26-2022, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T11:49:01-07:00","id":1487925,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it might be better to have the relevant Merit provide a bonus of rating/2 (rounded up), to keep in line with the usual Yantra bonuses.<br /> <br /> That being said, I would note that this is a Merit that becomes dependent on not only a prerequisite Merit but at least one other in order to do something. You get the first one of those for free at character creation fair enough, but I think obligating a person to buy an additional Merit to get the main effect out of this one is straining their points a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T13:55:54-07:00","id":1487935,"title":"","content":"Would like to point out that Investiture doesn't work that way (your Contacts and Staff don't convey a specific rank, title, or honor, which is why the Yantra normally keys off of Status or a Merit whose effects include &quot;dots in this Merit act as Status for the organization) and that High Speech and runes are &quot;more efficient&quot; Yantra <i>specifically because</i> they have drawbacks \u2014 per SoS's section on Storytelling Yantras, the bonus for stuff that's easy to get (like, say, the presence of Sleepers engaging in a practice with which you have regular-enough association to justify buying a Merit for using it as a magical focus) is +1.<br /> <br /> Spellcasting by default requires no gestures, words, or material components \u2014 as-written Techn\u00e9 effectively lets you treat &quot;ordinary people are doing knitting/mathematics/hoodoo&quot; as an Environment Yantra as long as the spell is something you could sneak into the effects of doing so, which is the point of the Free Council being more tied to Sleeper practices than the Diamond is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T14:37:07-07:00","id":1487939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1487789-an-alternative-techn\u00e9-merit?p=1487925#post1487925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it might be better to have the relevant Merit provide a bonus of rating/2 (rounded up), to keep in line with the usual Yantra bonuses.<br /> <br /> That being said, I would note that this is a Merit that becomes dependent on not only a prerequisite Merit but at least one other in order to do something. You get the first one of those for free at character creation fair enough, but I think obligating a person to buy an additional Merit to get the main effect out of this one is straining their points a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Investiture yantras normally add half of their merit rating, rounded up, as a yantra bonus. Did you perhaps mean that it shouldn't be called an Investiture or maybe that the bonus should be written explicitly in the writeup, making it more convenient to reference ?<br /> <br /> The <i>Lex Magica</i> requires the mage to already have points in SIlver Ladder or Concilium Status to work, so the required XP investment is a way to draw one more parallel between them. Without that, the mage still has access to the bonus from having Sleepers nearby practicing their foci. The ritual casting bonus is a way to follow up on the spirit of the original merit, which tried to incentivize groups into sharing a focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T03:32:05-07:00","id":1487998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1487789-an-alternative-techn\u00e9-merit?p=1487939#post1487939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Investiture yantras normally add half of their merit rating, rounded up, as a yantra bonus. Did you perhaps mean that it shouldn't be called an Investiture or maybe that the bonus should be written explicitly in the writeup, making it more convenient to reference ?</div> </div> </div> </div>You should probably write this kind of thing to be understandable to somebody who doesn't have Signs of Sorcery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>Lex Magica</i> requires the mage to already have points in SIlver Ladder or Concilium Status to work, so the required XP investment is a way to draw one more parallel between them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Lex Magica has at least one effect that doesn't key off Status, and that prereq Silver Ladder Status dot is given for free at character creation and can still be used in the Merit, so that one requires no further buy-in to get its minimum effect across the board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T16:41:58-07:00","id":1488225,"title":"","content":"I updated the description, adding the details about the yantra bonus. Currently I am not sure how to compensate for the required merit investment. One of the objectives is to maintain the mirror design with the Lex Magicka, creating 3 abilities that build upon each other. If the dice trick bonus was substituted for a yantra bonus proportional to the number of Sleepers practicing the focus, I think the sum of its parts would provide a weaker impression of Techn\u00e9 as an amplifier of teamwork spells. But if the bonus was added as one more feature, I think it would be too powerful for a 2 dot merit, even when considering that the Order specific ones tend to very strong in their specific niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}